{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":76331,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"243258b9-0512-5712-931a-df0906fd6600","total_cost_usd":0.6265380000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11896,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":7650,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11896,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7650,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11896},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6013,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006098,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":7650,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11896,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6204400000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-g1-reviewer-fable-32\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:58960ceebfb9cb96d1e0\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The workflow collapses the repeated session rows of each sapling into a single deficit mean and a single full mean per sapling before any statistical test, so repeated rows per independent unit never enter the test directly.\",\"observed_value\":\"one deficit mean and one full mean per sapling_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":44,\"end_line\":55,\"quoted_text\":\"def collapse_to_saplings(by_sapling):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Reduce repeated sessions to one deficit mean and one full mean per sapling.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    sapling_ids = sorted(by_sapling)\\n    deficit_means = []\\n    full_means = []\\n    for sapling in sapling_ids:\\n        regimes = by_sapling[sapling]\\n        if sorted(regimes) != [DEFICIT, FULL]:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"sapling \\\" + sapling + \\\" is missing an irrigation schedule\\\")\\n        deficit_means.append(average(regimes[DEFICIT]))\\n        full_means.append(average(regimes[FULL]))\\n    return sapling_ids, deficit_means, full_means\"}]},{\"description\":\"The statistical procedure is a paired t-test applied to the sapling-level regime means, with degrees of freedom computed as n_saplings - 1, so the analysed sample size equals the number of independent units (16), not the number of session rows (64).\",\"observed_value\":\"ttest_rel on 16 sapling-level means, df = 15\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":59,\"end_line\":67,\"quoted_text\":\"    n = len(sapling_ids)\\n    sessions_per_sapling = session_rows // n\\n    diffs = [d - f for d, f in zip(deficit_means, full_means)]\\n    mean_diff = average(diffs)\\n    sd_diff = math.sqrt(sum((d - mean_diff) ** 2 for d in diffs) / (n - 1))\\n    se_diff = sd_diff / math.sqrt(n)\\n    df = n - 1\\n\\n    test = stats.ttest_rel(deficit_means, full_means)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's stated degrees of freedom and test description are consistent with 16 independent saplings rather than 64 rows; independent recomputation from data/input.csv reproduces the reported values exactly (mean paired difference -24.00, SD 18.36, t(15) = -5.23, 95% CI [-33.78, -14.22]).\",\"observed_value\":\"t(15) = -5.23, p < 0.001, CI [-33.78, -14.22]; hand recomputation matches\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":21,\"end_line\":23,\"quoted_text\":\"- Mean within-sapling difference (deficit minus full): -24.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1 (SD 18.36)\\n- 95% CI for the mean difference: [-33.78, -14.22]\\n- Paired t-test: t(15) = -5.23, p < 0.001\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"Sessions repeated on the same sapling are not independent observations, so the 4\\nsessions belonging to a sapling were first collapsed into one deficit mean and one\\nfull mean for that sapling. The reported comparison is a two-sided paired t-test on\\nthe 16 sapling-level regime means, giving exactly one analysed row per sapling.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description confirms sapling_id is the independent unit and that four rows per sapling are repeated measurements of one plant, which is exactly the structure the workflow's aggregation step respects.\",\"observed_value\":\"Independent unit column: sapling_id; 4 rows per sapling are repeated measurements\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":31,\"end_line\":36,\"quoted_text\":\"Each sapling is its own pot with its own dripper and is the experimental unit of the\\nstudy. The four rows carrying the same sapling label are repeated measurements of one\\nplant, not measurements of four different plants.\\n\\nOne row is: one midday gas-exchange session on one potted olive sapling on one date\\nIndependent unit column: sapling_id\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The input file does contain repeated rows per independent unit (64 session rows, four per sapling, two per regime), so the hazard for this issue class is present in the raw data and had to be checked; the report also opens by citing all 64 sessions, which could superficially suggest row-level analysis.\",\"observed_value\":\"64 rows, 4 per sapling\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"Source: data/input.csv, 64 midday gas-exchange sessions recorded in\\nlong format. The 16 potted olive saplings were each measured on 4 dates: two sessions\\non the deficit schedule and two on the full schedule, in a counterbalanced crossover\\norder.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":13,\"end_line\":15,\"quoted_text\":\"The file is stored in long\\nformat: the four sessions of a sapling appear as four separate rows, so every sapling\\ncontributes four rows to the file.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to show the issue was present by (1) tracing every path from the CSV rows to the test call: read_sessions groups readings by sapling and regime, collapse_to_saplings averages within sapling-regime, and stats.ttest_rel receives only the 16-element deficit_means and full_means lists, so no code path feeds the 64 session rows into a row-independent procedure; and (2) recomputing the statistics by hand from data/input.csv under both the sapling-level analysis and a hypothetical row-level analysis. The sapling-level computation reproduces the report exactly (mean difference -24.00, SD 18.36, SE 4.589, t(15) = -5.23, 95% CI [-33.78, -14.22]), whereas a row-level paired test would have reported df = 31 and different dispersion values, which do not appear anywhere in the report. Both attempts failed to demonstrate the issue.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-g1-reviewer-fable-32","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:58960ceebfb9cb96d1e0","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow collapses the repeated session rows of each sapling into a single deficit mean and a single full mean per sapling before any statistical test, so repeated rows per independent unit never enter the test directly.","observed_value":"one deficit mean and one full mean per sapling_id","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":44,"end_line":55,"quoted_text":"def collapse_to_saplings(by_sapling):\n    \"\"\"Reduce repeated sessions to one deficit mean and one full mean per sapling.\"\"\"\n    sapling_ids = sorted(by_sapling)\n    deficit_means = []\n    full_means = []\n    for sapling in sapling_ids:\n        regimes = by_sapling[sapling]\n        if sorted(regimes) != [DEFICIT, FULL]:\n            raise ValueError(\"sapling \" + sapling + \" is missing an irrigation schedule\")\n        deficit_means.append(average(regimes[DEFICIT]))\n        full_means.append(average(regimes[FULL]))\n    return sapling_ids, deficit_means, full_means"}]},{"description":"The statistical procedure is a paired t-test applied to the sapling-level regime means, with degrees of freedom computed as n_saplings - 1, so the analysed sample size equals the number of independent units (16), not the number of session rows (64).","observed_value":"ttest_rel on 16 sapling-level means, df = 15","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":59,"end_line":67,"quoted_text":"    n = len(sapling_ids)\n    sessions_per_sapling = session_rows // n\n    diffs = [d - f for d, f in zip(deficit_means, full_means)]\n    mean_diff = average(diffs)\n    sd_diff = math.sqrt(sum((d - mean_diff) ** 2 for d in diffs) / (n - 1))\n    se_diff = sd_diff / math.sqrt(n)\n    df = n - 1\n\n    test = stats.ttest_rel(deficit_means, full_means)"}]},{"description":"The report's stated degrees of freedom and test description are consistent with 16 independent saplings rather than 64 rows; independent recomputation from data/input.csv reproduces the reported values exactly (mean paired difference -24.00, SD 18.36, t(15) = -5.23, 95% CI [-33.78, -14.22]).","observed_value":"t(15) = -5.23, p < 0.001, CI [-33.78, -14.22]; hand recomputation matches","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23,"quoted_text":"- Mean within-sapling difference (deficit minus full): -24.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1 (SD 18.36)\n- 95% CI for the mean difference: [-33.78, -14.22]\n- Paired t-test: t(15) = -5.23, p < 0.001"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":12,"end_line":15,"quoted_text":"Sessions repeated on the same sapling are not independent observations, so the 4\nsessions belonging to a sapling were first collapsed into one deficit mean and one\nfull mean for that sapling. The reported comparison is a two-sided paired t-test on\nthe 16 sapling-level regime means, giving exactly one analysed row per sapling."}]},{"description":"The data description confirms sapling_id is the independent unit and that four rows per sapling are repeated measurements of one plant, which is exactly the structure the workflow's aggregation step respects.","observed_value":"Independent unit column: sapling_id; 4 rows per sapling are repeated measurements","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":31,"end_line":36,"quoted_text":"Each sapling is its own pot with its own dripper and is the experimental unit of the\nstudy. The four rows carrying the same sapling label are repeated measurements of one\nplant, not measurements of four different plants.\n\nOne row is: one midday gas-exchange session on one potted olive sapling on one date\nIndependent unit column: sapling_id"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The input file does contain repeated rows per independent unit (64 session rows, four per sapling, two per regime), so the hazard for this issue class is present in the raw data and had to be checked; the report also opens by citing all 64 sessions, which could superficially suggest row-level analysis.","observed_value":"64 rows, 4 per sapling","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":8,"quoted_text":"Source: data/input.csv, 64 midday gas-exchange sessions recorded in\nlong format. The 16 potted olive saplings were each measured on 4 dates: two sessions\non the deficit schedule and two on the full schedule, in a counterbalanced crossover\norder."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":13,"end_line":15,"quoted_text":"The file is stored in long\nformat: the four sessions of a sapling appear as four separate rows, so every sapling\ncontributes four rows to the file."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to show the issue was present by (1) tracing every path from the CSV rows to the test call: read_sessions groups readings by sapling and regime, collapse_to_saplings averages within sapling-regime, and stats.ttest_rel receives only the 16-element deficit_means and full_means lists, so no code path feeds the 64 session rows into a row-independent procedure; and (2) recomputing the statistics by hand from data/input.csv under both the sapling-level analysis and a hypothetical row-level analysis. The sapling-level computation reproduces the report exactly (mean difference -24.00, SD 18.36, SE 4.589, t(15) = -5.23, 95% CI [-33.78, -14.22]), whereas a row-level paired test would have reported df = 31 and different dispersion values, which do not appear anywhere in the report. Both attempts failed to demonstrate the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":46794,"ttft_stream_ms":1908,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":76583,"uuid":"9280847b-b9e0-4934-a93a-57336ed71af3"}
